if there's one thing the hellraiser  franchise has taught us it's that you  should never mess with puzzle boxes as  horror fans already know the lament  configuration is the staple element of  the hellraiser movies and one of the  most iconic and enduring props from the  series acting as a bridge between our  world and that of the cenobytes now that  hulu's hellraiser reboot is finally here  the lament configuration is front and  center once again but this time it's  here in a wildly different shape the  newest hellraiser marks the 11th  installment in the franchise although  several movies in the series chose the  direct to video route understandably  fans have been freaking out over the  newest trailer for hulu's hellraiser  reimagining but many are wondering about  the lament configuration's strange shape  at the opening of the trailer  particularly since it then progresses to  become the cube we recognize from past  films considering the breadth of the  hellraiser franchise the lore and  history surrounding the lament  configuration is fairly robust the most  important feature of this demonic puzzle  box is that once an individual solves it  it creates a pathway between this world  and a dimension of untold pain and  madness the inhabitants of this evil  realm are usually referred to as  cenobytes each of them unique and frozen  in various states of ecstatic physical  torture but what each cenobite has in  common is that they're twisted into a  form of cruel mockery that represents a  person's mortal failings in some way and  above all don't open the box he needs  you to open the box but don't throughout  the series the lament configuration  usually takes the form of an  inconspicuous yet mysterious puzzle box  that often becomes an obsession for the  humans that gaze upon it however the  shape of this mystical object is not  fixed often once a lament configuration  is solved the box has a tendency to  unfurl quickly changing size and  appearance in a display of mechanical  perfection according to hellraiser lore  the lament configuration seen in the  movies thus far was originally created  in the 1700s by a french toymaker at the  behest of a noble person who was  obsessed with magic the noble thought  this puzzle box would grant him untold  powers with the ability to summon  cenobites for his own purposes however  it never works that way and summoning  these entities tends to result in  torture and death it's also important to  note that this is not the first nor only  lament configuration in fact in one of  the prior hellraiser movies there are  several on display not only is there  more than one lament configuration but  the design itself can be reversed to  trap the cenobites this was highlighted  in hellraiser bloodline where an entire  space station acts as an inverted lament  configuration that can trap and bind the  demons according to scary studies  original pinhead actor doug bradley once  explained you have to become aware of  the lament configurations and then you  have to find one and then solve the  puzzle it's not just the physical act of  opening the box it's the motivation  behind it  time to play another game  in essence there is indeed more than one  box and those boxes aren't necessarily  beholden to one specific shape and size  as a result it's perhaps not that  surprising that the lament configuration  has such a different shape in the first  moments of hulu's hellraiser trailer  perhaps this isn't the same lament  configuration previously featured  throughout the franchise or it could be  a different configuration of the puzzle  box entirely the rectangular form could  also represent an unopened state of the  configuration the trailer does mention  that there are six different  configurations to that one specific  puzzle box meanwhile director david  bruckner cautioned fans not to try to  place the new movie too directly into  existing hellraiser continuity telling  gizmodo i wouldn't say it's strict canon  again we let our imaginations run with  this my suggestion to fans is to go into  it not thinking exactly where it's  fitting in the history of the series and  to just experience the film regardless  lament configurations always result in  the same thing and that's suffering pain  and body horror truthfully when you have  a puzzle box that acts as a portal to a  demonic realm it probably isn't heavily  restricted by design or shape but the  outcome remains the same  [Music]  you
 

